-- =====================================================
-- GEOGRAPHIC MODEL DEFINITIONS
-- =====================================================

-- The Customer Geography dimension has one row per
-- normalized ZIP/city/state location combination.

-- Map-ready means the representative ZIP coordinate
-- passed the project's geographic screening rules.
-- It does not represent a verified customer address.

-- Customer geographic quality measures applied to
-- fact tables respond to Purchase Date, Order Status,
-- and other shared dimension filters.

-- Dimension-level location and seller counts do not
-- automatically respond to Purchase Date or Status
-- filtering because relationships are single-direction.

-- Missing references and flagged coordinates remain
-- in all business facts and overall KPI totals.

-- Seller reference-label disagreements are quality
-- indicators, not proof of incorrect physical addresses.

-- Fact-grain geographic counts must not be added
-- together as unique customers or unique orders.

